5. docker/libnvidia-api.so.1 is NOT original work.  It is a component that ships with
   the NVIDIA display driver (tested with driver 580.173.02, 720104 bytes).  It is
   included in this repository purely as an OFFLINE FALLBACK for the P-State power
   management path; that is a practical choice by this repository's publisher, not a
   licence grant.  It remains governed by the NVIDIA driver license, not by the Apache
   License above, and this project makes no claim that the NVIDIA license permits
   redistribution by third parties.
   Since package v1.2 this file is **opt-in**: the default is to bind the copy that comes
   with the host driver (run/start-here-v2.sh probes the three host library directories
   that upstream itself probes, and falls back to "no library + power.mode=sleep" when
   none is found).  The reason is measured, not theoretical: this pinned copy belongs to
   580.173.02, it is not owned by dpkg, and once the host driver moved to 580.178.04 the
   in-container pstate daemon died within 0.1 s with NVAPI_Initialize(): NVAPI_ERROR --
   i.e. a private copy goes silent exactly when the host driver drifts.  In the 0.1.7
   line this file is mounted read-only from the host and is never baked into an image.
   To use the bundled copy explicitly: NVAPI=package bash run/start-here-v2.sh
   To carry no P-State library at all:     NVAPI=none   bash run/start-here-v2.sh
   (power.mode then has to be "sleep" -- with "pstate" and no library the console throws
   BEFORE it spawns the engine, so the engine does not start at all; see
   docker/NVAPI-获取说明-v1.md).  Its integrity is pinned by sha256
   4a199f9b259a1098ab9c01d31c67f882a2531a0fbb9c3595ad3d016c7d131d8c
   (enforced for the bundled copy by docker/build.sh and run/start-here-v2.sh; a host
   driver's own copy is legitimately a different hash and is checked by path instead).
   See docker/NVAPI-获取说明-v1.md for how to obtain it from your own driver instead.
   Should NVIDIA (or the driver-pack licensor) object to this bundled copy, the publisher's
   stated intent is to drop the file from the repository and keep only the documented
   host-side path (probing the host driver's own library, or the sleep fallback) -- the
   package works without it, and that is why it is no longer the default.

